# UBOS Engineering Procedure

This repository is developed using milestone-based execution.

Do not skip milestones.

Do not combine multiple milestones.

Finish one milestone before beginning another.

---

# Required Reading

Before making changes read:

docs/handover/README.md

and all authoritative implementation documents.

---

# Required Workflow

Every engineering task shall follow exactly this sequence.

## Step 1

Understand the milestone objective.

Never assume.

Never redesign unrelated systems.

---

## Step 2

Reproduce the problem.

Evidence first.

No speculative fixes.

---

## Step 3

Identify the exact root cause.

Explain it before changing code.

---

## Step 4

Implement the smallest complete fix.

Prefer improving existing engines over creating new ones.

---

## Step 5

Execute validation.

Examples include:

- unit tests
- integration tests
- browser validation
- runtime validation
- FFmpeg validation
- API validation

---

## Step 6

Produce evidence.

Evidence always includes:

- commands executed
- runtime output
- artifacts
- screenshots when appropriate
- codecs
- durations
- paths
- exit codes

---

## Step 7

Prepare documentation updates.

When a milestone changes reality, prepare updates for:

- Product Truth
- Capability Matrix
- Subsystem Matrix
- Implementation Journal
- Completion Report
- Workflow State

Do not silently change documentation.

---

## Step 8

Create one focused commit.

Stop.

Do not continue into the next milestone.

---

# Definition of Done

Compilation is NOT completion.

Metadata is NOT completion.

Simulation is NOT completion.

A milestone is complete only when:

- operator action succeeds
- runtime succeeds
- external result succeeds
- evidence exists
- acceptance tests pass

---

# Reporting Format

Every milestone report must contain:

- Objective
- Root Cause
- Files Changed
- Commands Executed
- Test Results
- Runtime Evidence
- Artifact Evidence
- Cleanup Result
- Remaining Blockers
- Commit Hash
- PASS / PARTIAL / FAIL

---

# Engineering Philosophy

Build less.

Wire more.

Verify everything.

Never fake success.

Every feature must leave behind evidence.